{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/918214-let-s-talk-cartoons","id":918214,"title":"Let's Talk Cartoons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-20T13:16:52-07:00","id":918214,"title":"Let's Talk Cartoons","content":"Or, rather, cartoons that could be mined for ideas. I'm going to throw some out - I'll try to go for more obscure ones, because heaven only knows that you've probably seen the obvious ones.<br /> <br /> <b>Mona the Vampire</b> is a slice of my childhood... and probably a good look at what a light-hearted Innocents chronicle looks like. It's about a little girl who dresses up as a vampire and investigates mysteries <i>which she gives all kinds of supernatural explanations for</i>. The episodes flip-flop between how she sees things and what's &quot;really&quot; happening. I suggest it if you can still watch children's shows without spraining muscles from eye-rolling.<br /> <br /> <b>Detentionaire</b> is another good one to mine for ideas vis-a-vis an Innocents chronicle. The writers <i>clearly</i> had some fun with it, and it's well worth the watch. Let me tell you, the cyborg principal and live tatzlwurm mascot are the <i>tip</i> of the iceberg. It's <i>really</i> damn entertaining, is all I'm saying.<br /> <br /> <b>The Maxx</b>... Where to start? Well, say hello to the oneiros of Julie Winters. It's got bits and pieces for Changeling - though who the Changelings are is up for debate. Maxx pretty clearly <i>feels</i> like one of the Claimed, and Australia... &quot;Not the Australia they teach you about in the cities - the Outback. No, the *real* Australia: the smoking caves, the gods who eat mountains, the flying dragos, the rivers of gold, the Leopard Queen taunting me, almost an enemy, beautiful and feral as the great beasts she runs with.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you haven't seen it, MTV has the whole thing on their website. I strongly suggest it.<br /> <br /> <b>Cybersix</b> is... I've not checked the inspiration list for Deviant, but I'd <i>not</i> be surprised if Cybersix was on there. It even has the angst <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. It's been a while since I watched it, but it was a fun ride, and my gut is telling me that, yes, it was very World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <b>Delta State</b>: Stop me if you've heard this one before - four amnesiac psychics walk into a defensive war against voracious mental parasites from the deep human subconscious. Seriously, they have the Clairvoyance, Telepathy, Omen Sensitivity, and Object Reading merits, respectively, and have some merit that lets them enter the astral as a group. It's worth a watch, if only for the clever tricks for low-key psychics.<br /> <br /> So, anyone want to add to the list (I'm expecting to see someone suggest Gravity Falls or Over the Garden Wall. My hopes are a little lower for Monster Allergies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 06-20-2016, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T18:59:42-07:00","id":918362,"title":"","content":"I haven't watched these in a long time, so I'm relying on my memory and quick searches.<br /> <br /> <b>Gargoyles:</b> Not only is the atmosphere already excellent, the drama between the fascinating characters struck me as well-written even when I was too young to really know what that meant. I also remember fearing Xanatos a lot more than the Gargoyles, which is a testament to the former's cunning as an antagonist.<br /> <br /> <b>Ben10:</b> Despite being aimed at kids, the show had all sorts of fascinating ideas for aliens and assorted weirdness, and how they might adapt to life among humans. The Plumbers are a great inspirational material for Conspiracies. Some episodes have pretty dark stuff as well, but it never lost sight of the humor and the Rule Of Cool. I haven't seen the sequel series, so I can't recommend those. Ben himself could be seen as a Deviant, since he has an implanted gadget with strange and visually obvious powers that motivates several people and monsters to hunt him down.<br /> <br /> <b>Godzilla:</b> No, not the one with Godzooky. I'm talking about the one based on the 1998 American adaptation that got terrible reviews. It has <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EbfmC7_CdK4\" target=\"_blank\"><b>a kick-ass intro</b></a>, and some cool ideas for how the CoD might respond to kaiju threats and allies. The designs for the kaiju themselves are pretty great too.<br /> <br /> <b>Batman The Animated Series:</b> Seriously, I'm putting this one here as more of an &quot;inb4&quot;. If you want some inspiration for a vigilante Hunter game, look no further.<br /> <br /> I didn't know you liked cartoons, Amechra. Do you happen to frequent /co/ and /tg/?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-21-2016, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T19:10:26-07:00","id":918365,"title":"","content":"Oh, I forgot to mention <b>Courage The Cowardly Dog</b>, for its surreal brand of horror and humor. It's a goldmine of inspiration for creepy mysteries and Horrors, but my favorites antagonist is Katz, who strikes me as possible inspiration for a recurring Slasher. Courage himself often uses something like the Tactics of Hunters, as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-20-2016, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T19:15:59-07:00","id":918367,"title":"","content":"Nope, I'm &quot;independently taught&quot;, and kinda prefer not to get into the ultra-close discussion of them.<br /> <br /> (Also, I was never able to get into Gargoyles - I think it's my fault for watching Freekazoid's parody before the actual show.)<br /> <br /> Also, if we're talking Hunter - <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iF9BMc3rVA0\" target=\"_blank\">here's</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pXHeuRMc6ak\" target=\"_blank\">some</a>. <i>That's</i> is what it looks like at the Conspiracy level. (On a much more terrible note, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7mZEcUCVT6w\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> is what a <i>bad</i> Conspiracy level game looks like.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T19:28:52-07:00","id":918372,"title":"","content":"There was a short lived show that Disney had called <b>Filmore </b>that is a absolutely great source of inspiration for how to portray an interesting chase in an innocents game, with multiple foot chases per episode as a result of the series being a send up of 70s police procedurals starring a middle safety patrol. The show is hard to find though, there seems to some issue with the rights to some of the music used in the show that keeps Disney from releasing it on dvd or streaming.<br /> <br /> <b>Scooby Doo Mystery Incorporated</b> is what happens when you take a tongue in cheek version of the classic scooby doo formula, add an ongoing plot that draws inspiration from horror genre sources ranging from classic horror movies to Babylonian mythology to HP Lovecraft in ways both serious and parodic with a big spoonful of interpersonal drama between the mystery inc gang for good measure. This is very much a darker and grittier scooby doo, to the point where the costumed villains actually try to kill the gang rather than limiting themselves to trying to scare. Perfect for the chronicles of darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T19:29:10-07:00","id":918373,"title":"","content":"<b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Todd_McFarlane%27s_Spawn\" target=\"_blank\">Spawn</a></b> certainly has the dark imagery and mystery of the Chronicles of Darkness. It arguably takes it too far, you might be surprised they didn't run out of black ink, but the representation of mood and atmosphere is solid.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%86on_Flux\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Aeon Flux</b></a> could probably be a good inspiration for a particularly frenetic mortal game, Hunter with a large espionage component, or more likely Demon.<br /> <br /> A lot of strides have been made in taking cartoons from a series of unconnected episodes to having episodes that are each important parts of a larger story, whether they move against the larger metaplot or show characters developing in response to previous episodes. It's not unheard of to build chronicles like seasons from tv shows. Dragon Magazine did an article about it long, long ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-20-2016, 10:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T19:38:54-07:00","id":918378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/918214-let-s-talk-cartoons?p=918367#post918367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, I'm &quot;independently taught&quot;, and kinda prefer not to get into the ultra-close discussion of them.<br /> <br /> (Also, I was never able to get into Gargoyles - I think it's my fault for watching Freekazoid's parody before the actual show.)<br /> <br /> Also, if we're talking Hunter - <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iF9BMc3rVA0\" target=\"_blank\">here's</a> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pXHeuRMc6ak\" target=\"_blank\">some</a>. <i>That's</i> is what it looks like at the Conspiracy level. (On a much more terrible note, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7mZEcUCVT6w\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> is what a <i>bad</i> Conspiracy level game looks like.)</div> </div> </div> </div> I remember seeing that intro for MIB and posting it on the Deviant thread, but I didn't mention it here because I didn't actually watch the show. I hadn't heard of this Roswell Conspiracies, it looks badass. As for Huntik, I had to force myself to watch the intro to the end. It sounds almost like a parody to me.<br /> <br /> Have you seen any of the shows I mentioned so far, and if so, what did you think about them? I'm trying to remember episodes from <b>Jackie Chan Adventures</b>, but I'm failing pretty hard.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't it be awesome if there was a Hellboy Animated Series that was faithful to the comics?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T19:44:07-07:00","id":918383,"title":"","content":"Detentionaire is one continuous plot for 53 episodes - there aren't <i>any</i> filler episodes (what? I just finished marathoning it, so it's in the forefront of my mind).<br /> <br /> And I remember Filmore - didn't remember the name, though. Those were <i>great</i> chases. As for another Disney one, the <i>Lilo &amp; Stitch</i> cartoon would be great for a mortal-level game.<br /> <br /> <i>Interstella 5555</i> is a good movie for Changeling. As is <i>The Halloween Tree</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T20:04:47-07:00","id":918393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/918214-let-s-talk-cartoons?p=918378#post918378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I remember seeing that intro for MIB and posting it on the Deviant thread, but I didn't mention it here because I didn't actually watch the show. I hadn't heard of this Roswell Conspiracies, it looks badass. As for Huntik, I had to force myself to watch the intro to the end. It sounds almost like a parody to me.<br /> <br /> Have you seen any of the shows I mentioned so far, and if so, what did you think about them? I'm trying to remember episodes from <b>Jackie Chan Adventures</b>, but I'm failing pretty hard.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't it be awesome if there was a Hellboy Animated Series that was faithful to the comics?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen a bit of Gargoyles and Ben10. As for Roswell Conspiracies - it is ridiculously awesome, in the way only a show about a badass secret agent and his banshee partner can be.<br /> <br /> Huntik, on the other hand, is Indiana Jones meets Pokemon with kung-fu, if the main characters had a home base in Venice. The first season isn't so bad if you don't think too hard about it; the second season is <i>complete and utter trash</i>, and possibly the only case of negative character development I've ever seen (at least at that scale - you know, retroactively making one character's father figure the in-setting equivalent of Josef Mengele was <i>probably</i> a bad idea).<br /> <br /> But, being a little silly... Innocents + Mage = <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mn1SgEYEoCM\" target=\"_blank\">Sabrina the Teenage Witch</a>. Every episode includes an important lesson on Wisdom! Like &quot;don't open up random grimoires and sing the contents at your school talent show&quot;, &quot;it might be a bad idea to bring adorable baby monsters home&quot;, &quot;stop abusing your timeline, you idiot&quot;, and &quot;no, casting love spells on one of your teachers because they look lonely is not a good idea.&quot; Some of those might have been the <i>other</i> series (not the one from the 70s or the new one, neither of which I've seen. Yes, there have been four. No, I'm not sure why Archie Comics and derived properties are amazing.)<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> And yes, yes it would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T20:05:30-07:00","id":918394,"title":"","content":"Has anyone else seen <b>The Real Ghostbusters</b>? It had the same characteristic style of the movie, and they went on to bust more than just ghosts. They had to get clever when facing these monsters that were outside their area of expertise, which made the episodes more interesting. There was even one where they banished Cthulhu. It had a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=M7VS-ZoeMqs\" target=\"_blank\"><b>cool intro</b></a>, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T20:21:30-07:00","id":918399,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a>, your comments about Sabrina made me remember 3 similar shows starring badass girls: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h5lvn2GRXSY\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Juniper Lee</b></a>, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W86QOeHiqTk\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Kim Possible</b></a> and <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=49WPb5XYvac\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Life As A Teenage Robot.</b></a> The first is more like Mage, the second is Hunters + Genius and the third has some Promethean vibes.<br /> <br /> Also, is it just me, or is <b>Powerpuff Girls</b> totally Innocents + Deviant? The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Powerpuff_Girls_Movie\" target=\"_blank\"><b>movie</b></a> is a lot more serious about the Deviant part, but the cartoon had some messed up stuff as well, like that zombie stage magician and the mime who stole all colors and joy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T15:00:23-07:00","id":918819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/918214-let-s-talk-cartoons?p=918367#post918367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I was never able to get into Gargoyles - I think it's my fault for watching <b>Freekazoid's </b>parody before the actual show.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Duh. <a href=\"http://villains.wikia.com/wiki/Candlejack\" target=\"_blank\">Candle Jack</a>. Can't believe I di","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T16:28:28-07:00","id":918845,"title":"","content":"Danny Phantom is a really good cartoon that could make for good Geist inspiration","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T17:12:38-07:00","id":918867,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Secret_Saturdays\" target=\"_blank\">The Secret Saturdays</a>: A whole family of hunters specialized in dealing with cryptids (having even adopted several of them).<br /> Note: special points for being one of the few cartoons with a teen main character who uses his cunning more often than superpowers. Shame on you, Ben Tennyson.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T08:11:21-07:00","id":919094,"title":"","content":"<b>Gravity Falls</b> is excellent in its own right, as well as having some excellent inspiration for ChroD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T10:09:28-07:00","id":996130,"title":"","content":"Necro because the Murphys are clearly an Acanthus Proximi dynasty with the curse of being a walking disaster area<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ARTRJQfV90k\" data-code=\"ARTRJQfV90k\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ARTRJQfV90k/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T14:32:26-07:00","id":996265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/918214-let-s-talk-cartoons?p=919094#post919094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Gravity Falls</b> is excellent in its own right, as well as having some excellent inspiration for ChroD.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have heard it described as &quot;Twin Peaks for Kids&quot;, which does make it tempting. I've yet to watch it, though.<br /> <br /> Rick and Morty is pretty much the quintessential &quot;Low-Obligation Genius&quot; if we care at all about fangames.<br /> <br /> Over the Garden Wall is great for Changeling, if you're willing to look at the Unknown as an unusually well-populated part of the Hedge. It works so well that the Unknown has pretty much become what I model the Hedge off of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T15:01:57-07:00","id":996282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/918214-let-s-talk-cartoons?p=996265#post996265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rick and Morty is pretty much the quintessential &quot;Low-Obligation Genius&quot; if we care at all about fangames.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Morty's a great inspiartion for a Genius who successfully completed his charachter development. Obviously Morty isn't a Genius (which is probably why he <i>Gets It </i>but he's still great inspiration). Really the whole family is great inspiration for showing so many different reactions to powerlessness in a vast uncaring cosmos.<br /> <br /> Anyway the <b>Beetlejuice </b>cartoon would be a good inspiration for a Sin-Eater game.<br /> <br /> <b>W.I.T.C.H.</b> Makes great inspiration for Princess or Mage. (Season 1 is ok, 2 is much better. I'm talking about 2 here). For Princess has themes of social responsibility, power of love, and fighting fear. For Mage it goes into power corrupts. I can't say more without spoilers.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T15:16:20-07:00","id":996291,"title":"","content":"Promethean :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TsOJy8Yub4c\" data-code=\"TsOJy8Yub4c\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/TsOJy8Yub4c/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T16:13:44-07:00","id":996313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/918214-let-s-talk-cartoons?p=996265#post996265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have heard it described as &quot;Twin Peaks for Kids&quot;, which does make it tempting. I've yet to watch it, though.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It really is good. They really manage to capture that pacific northwest weirdness well and a lot of the episodes are pretty much shout outs to famous horror or conspiracy stories.<br /> <br /> Also, am I the only one who thinks Ms. Frizzle is part of some Thyrsus legacy (the once and future teachers?) based on the &quot;once and future king&quot; version of the king Arthur story, using magic and transformation to teach her students, who will grow up to be important, lessons that will help them in their futures?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T18:18:28-07:00","id":996372,"title":"","content":"I like [b]Gargoyles, Ben10, 98's Godzilla (it went a lot better than that trashy movie) and Batman Animated Series. Really inspirational for a lot of games in the CoD style.<br /> <br /> Courage, The Cowardly Dog strikes me as being in the CoD setting, if in a Shard with talking animals. And that computer is certainly a cryptid of some kind.<br /> <br /> MiB is a classic for the modern Conspiracy, and the first story that I know (and remember now) were these Men In Black are actually the good guys. It was one of the greater inspirations for the Revised-era Technocracy and some conspiracies in CoD.<br /> <br /> Roswell Conspiracies seemed pretty good, but it didn't went for too long here were I live, so I didn't saw more than 3 episodes. And later forget to look for more, maybe I'll do it later.<br /> <br /> Scooby Doo Mystery Incorporated is a lot of material to use, but actually any Scooby Doo series can be used for a lot of inspiration. Even being a parody of the Gothic genre, they're one of the most complete examples of it, and also of the best. There is bound to be a reason for Scooby Doo being the most successful cartoon in history.<br /> <br /> I remember a lot of Jackie Chan Adventures, but it is actually far more food for Pulp Action than Horror, though it go fairly well with Mage. The same can be said of Xiaolin Showdown.<br /> <br /> Both The Real Ghostbusters and Extreme Ghostbusters are very good, indeed. By the way, the episode where they face Great Cthulhu on Real Ghostbusters does have a continuation on Extreme Ghostbusters.<br /> <br /> Good to remember Juniper Lee, and I kinda liked My Life As A Teenage Robot, and certainly loved to watch Powerpuff Girls. Also Danny Phantom did a fairly good job. But Kim Possible wasn't my game.<br /> <br /> And The Secret Saturdays, honestly, it strikes me as a really bad copy of another classic: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_ZU0uFgrhr0\" target=\"_blank\">Jonny Quest</a>. It was to the Pulp genre almost what Scooby Doo was to the Gothic. Gravity Falls I going to watch later tonight.<br /> <br /> You certainly can draw a lot for Sin-Eater from Beetlejuice, but also a lot of inspiration can be taken from <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6wXcwB17IW4\" target=\"_blank\">The Grim Adventures of Billy And Mandy</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T21:05:28-07:00","id":996433,"title":"","content":"An odd suggestion (less ChroD related, but still <i>excellent</i>):<br /> <br /> Who here has seen <i>Wakfu</i>? If not, watch it - it's definite inspiration for Exalted/Scion in <i>feel</i>, though I feel Sadlygrove's relationship with Rubilax has some <i>excellent</i> stuff to steal (I'm surprised &quot;wielders of demonically-infused relics, both as jailers and warriors&quot; isn't a Hunter conspiracy). This is not about <i>Wakfu</i>\u00b9.<br /> <br /> No, this is about the mini-spinoff for kids, <i>Dofus: The Treasures of Kerubim Crespin</i>. The series is about a grandfather telling his grandson about the adventures of his youth - because how do you <i>think</i> his item shop got stocked? Over the course of the series, you learn that, while the events he's sharing are <i>true</i>, they aren't exactly what <i>happened</i>.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> For a more pertinent ones - I suggest <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=koesW3xMKtY\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Megas XLR</i></a> for a light-hearted chronicle, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hgwSpajMw3s\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Paranorman</i></a> as <i>stupidly good</i> Sin Eater inspiration, and I can't wait for the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6XEaAaLRVYo\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Zombillenium</i></a> movie to be out. Also <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HnMnOSU2S5Q\" target=\"_blank\">Xiaolin Showdown</a> is... just watch it. That's my next Hunter chronicle (well, most of the characters are Hunters. Wuya is, I would guess, an Earthbound True Fae).<br /> <br /> Seriously, though, <i>Paranorman</i> has one of the <i>best</i> &quot;help a ghost move on&quot; scenes I've seen.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">\u00b9 I will talk about how Wakfu is one of the best works of Western animation of the last 10 years on request, though<i>.</i></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 11-01-2016, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T01:32:02-07:00","id":996495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/918214-let-s-talk-cartoons?p=996433#post996433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An odd suggestion (less ChroD related, but still <i>excellent</i>):<br /> <br /> Who here has seen <i>Wakfu</i>? If not, watch it - it's definite inspiration for Exalted/Scion in <i>feel</i>, though I feel Sadlygrove's relationship with Rubilax has some <i>excellent</i> stuff to steal (I'm surprised &quot;wielders of demonically-infused relics, both as jailers and warriors&quot; isn't a Hunter conspiracy). This is not about <i>Wakfu</i>\u00b9.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wakfu is awesome.<br /> <br /> Nox is great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T06:28:57-07:00","id":996552,"title":"","content":"Definitely not a cartoon for kids, but I would like to put in a recommendation for a horror anime called Another. It has a very interesting plot to it, which I won't spoil, but I only wish that I could run a game that had that kind of a feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T11:53:13-07:00","id":996723,"title":"","content":"<b>Justice League </b>and <b>Justice League: Unlimited</b> are good inspiration for a lighter shade of the CoD, but when it comes to inspiration there's nothing better than CADMUS for a Hunter conspiracy, as well as Grodd's Legion of Doom for a worst-case scenario; the various evil-types grouping together.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T15:09:42-07:00","id":996830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/918214-let-s-talk-cartoons?p=996495#post996495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wakfu is awesome.<br /> <br /> Nox is great.</div> </div> </div> </div>His theme is amazing:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h-kp5JfhEaw\" data-code=\"h-kp5JfhEaw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/h-kp5JfhEaw/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T02:16:09-07:00","id":997617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/918214-let-s-talk-cartoons?p=996313#post996313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really is good. They really manage to capture that pacific northwest weirdness well and a lot of the episodes are pretty much shout outs to famous horror or conspiracy stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably the fan in me talking, but I can't help but see Gravity Falls as a Mage chronicle. It's not tough to see how obsessions, mysteries, and a supernatural past figure into the plot. Uncovering the truth requires extensive digging. Nothing is as it seems at a first or even second glance. And you might not like what you find out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7925,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7925-rdmarquis","user":"RdMarquis","date":". 11-03-2016, 05:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7925-rdmarquis","name":"RdMarquis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T23:04:21-08:00","id":1005616,"title":"","content":"I just realized that Rodger from American Dad is either the best demon of the tempter agenda or the worst, but given <a href=\"https://youtu.be/mX2Hy98v0dQ?t=2m2s\" target=\"_blank\">how many covers h</a>e has, I would say he is at least competent at making soul pacts.<br /> <br /> And also, that scene I linked would be a very interesting thing for a demon to deal with, a whole army of all their covers swarming over them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 11-20-2016, 02:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":